  "problem": "The equation of the hyperbola $7{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}=84$ in standard form is{{field-1}}\n$=1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $84$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =84 \\\\ \\frac{7{y}^{2}}{84}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{84} & =\\frac{84}{84} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{28} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
